    "done_when": "docs/research/data/local-lane-deaths.json exists, at most 200 KB, and carries a before block. The block gives the window, the population, the count of deaths at the review reflex's effort, and a named positive control whose death the parser sees.\n\ntests/test_the_local_lane_death_rate_is_stated.py reads only that committed file. It asserts that the before block's death count is non-zero and that the positive control is present and classified as a death. If an after block exists, it asserts the same shape for it.\n\nBefore the change the data file is absent and the test fails at load. After the change the gate `/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q tests/test_the_local_lane_death_rate_is_stated.py`, run from the worktree, exits 0.\n\ndocs/research/local-lane-death-rate.html exists as a reckon-type=doc page embedding the figure from docs/figures/the-orchestrator-lane-is-not-a-worker-lane/. The stream scan is bounded to 20 minutes of wall time and runs as `timeout 1200 ...`.",
